WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.300
The first trailer for Marvel's The Avengers:
Infinity War has finally dropped, and it's

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.290
as much of a doozy as fans might've expected.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:13.370
Not only do we finally see the many new subsets
of superheroes come together with the OG Avengers,

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:19.060
but Thanos has finally decided to step down
from his space throne and take a shot at gathering

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.239
those Infinity Stones.

00:00:20.239 --> 00:00:23.730
And, from the looks of this trailer, he's
off to a good start.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:28.229
Let's take a look at some of the finer details
you might've missed in the trailer for Avengers:

00:00:28.229 --> 00:00:30.099
Infinity War.

00:00:30.099 --> 00:00:31.479
Loki's betrayal

00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:36.620
The events of Thor: Ragnarok might've brought
Thor and Loki to a cheeky detente, but it

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:41.650
was just a matter of time before brother dearest
betrayed that newly-earned trust.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:46.280
This new trailer shows Loki handing over the
Tesseract to someone who is probably Thanos

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.960
or one of his minions.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:52.330
And if that isn't bad enough, it also shows
him stepping over a bunch of bodies to do

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:53.330
so.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:57.900
Could that giant ship that arrived in the
bleak mid-credits scene after Ragnarok truly

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.280
have heralded Thanos' arrival?

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.700
And if so, will it mean the destruction of
the remaining Asgardians?

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.880
Thor does seem pretty broken up in the glimpses
we get of him here.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.960
He's sporting a patch to conceal the damage
Hela did to his eye in Ragnarok, and he seems

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.490
to be trying to fight something well above
his pay grade by pushing against the levers

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.219
on some massive machine.

00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:21.500
He's later shown looking through a spaceship
window, which might be on the Guardians' Milano.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.100
And when he does finally meet Star-Lord and
his alien crew, Thor seems lonelier and more

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.609
contemptuous than ever.

00:01:27.609 --> 00:01:31.900
If our hunch is right about Loki, it's not
hard to guess why Thor would be in such a

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.499
bad mood.

00:01:33.499 --> 00:01:35.039
A new villain?

00:01:35.039 --> 00:01:39.270
There are two flashes in the Avengers: Infinity
War trailer that point to a new villain.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:43.750
In one, Captain America, all decked out in
black and bearded, is shown tussling with

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:48.439
someone who looks a lot like Proxima Midnight,
a member of Thanos' Black Order.

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:53.499
Then, we see poor Vision having his head zapped
by a golden staff that looks an awful lot

00:01:53.499 --> 00:01:56.520
like the one owned by Corvus Glaive in the
comics.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.460
This grim reaper-esque villain is a faithful
servant of Thanos, a member of his Black Order,

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:05.889
and is known for having a magical connection
to his glaive's blade, which appears to do

00:02:05.889 --> 00:02:07.659
his terrible bidding against Vision here.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:08.659
Since Thanos is on a mission to collect Infinity
Stones—and Vision possesses the Mind Stone—we

00:02:08.659 --> 00:02:09.659
might be looking at the first member of his
new hit squad here, even if we barely see

00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:10.659
his face.

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:11.659
Spidey's new digs

00:02:11.659 --> 00:02:14.560
It looks like Spider-Man plays a big part
in trying to shut down the portal … or whatever

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.870
that device that's hanging over the city will
be called.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:21.550
And he'll be doing so in his fancy new "Iron
Spider" suit—and that's not the only thing

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.580
that's new about Spider-Man in this movie.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:28.310
He's also shown on a school bus experiencing
his spider-sense in the form of raised arm

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:32.450
hair, which alerts him to the fact that the
city's just been invaded by the looming sky

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.100
ring of doom.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.790
Wakanda here we come

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:40.710
Avengers: Infinity War won't be the first
film to make landfall in Wakanda, of course,

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:44.300
since we first saw the country in Civil War's
mid-credits scene.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.100
Black Panther's release date precedes the
Infinity War by several months as well.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:52.300
But it does look like the gang will recruit
T'Challa and Okoye to join their superhero

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.650
squad—there are several glimpses of Wakanda
throughout the trailer, including one big

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:01.900
battle that'll feature Captain America, the
Winter Soldier, the Black Widow, Hulk, and

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:02.900
more.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:06.380
Guess Bruce isn't having trouble transitioning
back and forth into Hulk the way he feared

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:09.300
he might be in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.800
Hand-to-hand

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.980
Although Thanos has been a pretty hands-off
kind of space villain until now, he decided

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:18.620
in the mid-credits scene for Avengers: Age
of Ultron that he was going to take matters

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:22.510
into his own hands before gloving up with
the then-unjeweled Infinity Gauntlet.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:26.740
And it looks like he's going to make good
on that promise in Avengers: Infinity War,

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.380
because he's shown personally bringing the
pain to some of our heroes.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.950
Chief among his victims is Spider-Man who
seems to take quite a beating from our intergalactic

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:35.950
baddie.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:39.240
Of course, the final showdown will probably
be a little more spectacular than either of

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.360
these clips, but it's still clearly very personal
for Thanos right now.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.080
Speaking of which …

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.060
Thanos has stones

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:51.620
Before this movie, it wasn't clear that Thanos
would have any Infinity Stones to add to his

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.720
Gauntlet, or whether he'd even gotten the
real Gauntlet this time.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:59.330
As expected, though, the fact that it's on
his left hand now shows that it is not only

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:02.910
the real deal, but he's been able to add at
least two stones to it.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:06.610
The first stone is purple, which seems to
indicate that he's retrieved the Power Stone

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:11.340
Ronan tried to keep for himself in Guardians
of the Galaxy, but which ended up securely

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.200
at Nova Corps headquarters.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.600
The second is blue, which probably means it's
the Space Stone Loki is shown passing along

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.600
earlier.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.920
We don't know if he'll be able to gather the
yellow Mind Stone from Vision, or the green

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:27.100
Time Stone from Doctor Strange … but he's
still farther along in his quest than many

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.170
fans might've expected by now.

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:34.020
There was a leaked teaser image in 2014 that
indicated Thanos would eventually gather all

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.350
of the stones at some point, but it's not
clear whether that'll happen in this movie,

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:40.770
or in Avengers Four, which is due in 2019.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:45.380
One thing we do know is that it'll all add
up to a heck of a fight for our heroes—one

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:50.130
that's destined to end in what Marvel chief
Kevin Feige has described as "a finale" for

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.030
the MCU as we know it.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:53.030
Thanks for watching!

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:55.710
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.810
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

